            <ArticleTitle>Bifrontal headache · blurred vision · vomiting · Dx?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>358-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 55-year-old woman presented to the emergency department (ED) with a bifrontal headache that she'd had for one day. She also had blurred vision and was vomiting shortly before coming to the hospital. The patient had no history of hypertension, migraine headaches, seizure disorder, autoimmune disorders, or cerebrovascular disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
